kosha calcium

  -- Ca. proton-20. period 4, group 2 alkaline earth. valence: 2.
  -- most abundant mineral in the human body — 99% in bones and teeth (hydroxyapatite).
  -- Ca²⁺ ion: muscle contraction signal, neurotransmitter release, blood clotting.
  -- CaCO3: limestone, marble, chalk, seashells. CaSO4: gypsum, plaster.
  -- concrete: calcium silicate hydrate from cement (CaO) + SiO2 + H2O.
  -- Ca²⁺ is the second messenger — signal amplification inside cells.

